data: {"type": "text_delta_finish", "role": "text", "content": "The documentation does not provide a complete side-by-side setup flow for connecting **WhatsApp** and **Instagram** channels.\n\nWhat it does document:\n\n- **Instagram:** Configure channel-specific handling through **Autoresponders**:\n  1. Open the **Welcome Journey** and **Fallback Journey**.\n  2. Add a **Condition** node after **Starting**.\n  3. Select the system variable `channel`.\n  4. Route Instagram users to the appropriate journey.\n- **WhatsApp:** The available documentation does not specify the initial account connection, credentials, or channel activation steps.\n- **Instagram-specific options:** It documents unlinking the Instagram account and configuring the Persistent Menu.\n\nTherefore, the documented difference is that Instagram has explicit journey-routing guidance, while the WhatsApp onboarding steps are not covered in the available documentation.\n\nSource: `kb/channels/autoresponders.md`"}

